hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"82","Allāhumma innī as'aluka `ilman nāfi`an, wa rizqan ṭayyiban, wa `amalam-mutaqabbala. ¤ ---------------------------------¤ [to be said after giving salam for the Fajr prayer.] ""O Allah, I ask You for knowledge which is beneficial, and sustenance which is good, and deeds which are acceptable."
